# Everything in this repository runs inside a Linux container, so everything in
# it is checked out with LF endings regardless of the host committing it.
#
# This is not tidiness. A shell script with CRLF endings fails inside the image
# in a way that reads as nonsense: the kernel takes `#!/bin/bash\r` literally and
# reports "no such file or directory" naming an interpreter that plainly exists,
# and any line that survives that carries a stray \r into every variable it sets.
# The repository is authored on Windows, where git's default would introduce
# exactly that on checkout.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

Dockerfile       text eol=lf
passwd.template  text eol=lf

LICENSE text eol=lf
